Hi Evan

I think that's not a bad idea at all.

On the other hand, I don't know how easy it is to fix the survival parameter in unmarked. And, more importantly, the Bayesian approach would look ideal for such a combination of information, in that you can rigorously incorporate into estimation not only your best guess of the parameter (i.e., say the MLE from the cap-recapture analysis) but also the uncertainty, i.e., the standard error by forming a prior in BUGS of the form phi ~ Normal(MLE, 1/(SE*SE)).

Kind regards  --  Marc

